---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import GuideHeader from "../../components/help/GuideHeader.astro";
import GuideNav from "../../components/help/GuideNav.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/help/Callout.astro";
import Steps from "../../components/help/Steps.astro";
import RelatedGuides from "../../components/help/RelatedGuides.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "choose", label: "Pickup or delivery" },
  { id: "time", label: "The delivery time" },
  { id: "track", label: "Following your order" },
  { id: "confirm", label: "Confirming it arrived" },
  { id: "late", label: "If it is late" },
  { id: "problem", label: "If something is wrong" },
  { id: "unpaid", label: "Unpaid orders" },
];
---

<Page
  title="Delivery and your orders"
  description="Pickup or delivery, the delivery time sellers promise, tracking an order, confirming it arrived and what to do if it is late."
>
  <GuideHeader
    title="Delivery and your orders"
    intro="How getting your item works, and what to do if it does not go to plan."
  />
  <GuideNav items={sections} />

  <article class="guide">
    <section id="choose">
      <h2>Pickup or delivery</h2>
      <p>
        When you pay, choose how you want to get your item. If a seller
        delivers, you will see <strong>Delivery</strong> next to{" "}
        <strong>Pickup</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pickup:</strong> no extra cost. Arrange a time and place with the seller in the chat.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> the seller sends it to you. Their delivery fee is shown before you pay, and added to the total.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can change between the two in the cart or on the pay screen, before you pay.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="time">
      <h2>The delivery time</h2>
      <p>
        For a delivery, the seller tells you how many days it will take{" "}
        <strong>before you pay</strong>. It is always <strong>at least 2
        days</strong>, and it is counted from the day you pay. You agree to it
        by paying.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once you have paid, your order shows <strong>Delivery promised
        by</strong> and the date, so you always know what to expect.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="track">
      <h2>Following your order</h2>
      <p>Open the <strong>Orders</strong> tab to see all your orders. Each one shows where it stands:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pending:</strong> paid, and the seller is getting it ready</li>
        <li><strong>On its way / Delivered:</strong> the seller has sent it or handed it over</li>
        <li><strong>Completed:</strong> you confirmed it arrived</li>
        <li><strong>Disputed:</strong> a problem was reported, and our team is looking into it</li>
        <li><strong>Refunded, Cancelled or Expired:</strong> the order ended without a sale</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You are also notified about each step, and you can open the chat with
        the seller from any order.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="confirm">
      <h2>Confirming it arrived</h2>
      <p>
        When your item arrives and looks right, open the order and tap{" "}
        <strong>Received</strong>. You will be asked to confirm, because
        confirming pays the seller. Then you can leave them a rating.
      </p>
      <Callout title="Do not forget to confirm" tone="safety">
        <p>
          If you neither confirm nor report a problem, the order completes on
          its own a few days after the promised delivery date, and the seller is
          paid. Check your item soon after it arrives.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="late">
      <h2>If it is late</h2>
      <p>
        The seller says they sent it, but it has not reached you? Open the
        order and tap <strong>Not arrived yet</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The seller is told to check on your delivery.</li>
        <li>The order waits 4 more days before it can complete on its own.</li>
        <li>You can do this up to two times. After that, report a problem if it still has not arrived.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="problem">
      <h2>If something is wrong</h2>
      <p>
        The item never came, is not what was described, or is damaged? Open the
        order and tap <strong>Report a problem</strong>. Describe what happened
        in a sentence or two.
      </p>
      <Steps
        items={[
          {
            title: "You report it",
            body: "The order is marked as disputed, so the seller is not paid while it is looked at.",
          },
          {
            title: "Our team reviews it",
            body: "We read your report, the order details and the recent messages between you and the seller.",
          },
          {
            title: "We decide",
            body: "If you were let down, the order is refunded. If the seller did everything right, the order is completed in their favour.",
          },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section id="unpaid">
      <h2>Unpaid orders</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>When you start to pay, the item is held for you for about 30 minutes. If the payment is not completed, it is released for other buyers.</li>
        <li>You can have up to three unpaid orders open at the same time.</li>
        <li>An order you have not paid for can be cancelled at any time from your Orders.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <RelatedGuides current="delivery-and-orders" />
  </article>
</Page>
